    "title": "Bill Murray Cheers On UConn in 2026 Final Four - Storrs Today",
    "text": "Got story updates? Submit your updates here. ›Bill Murray, the acclaimed actor, has become a fixture at UConn Huskies men's basketball games in recent years. The reason? Murray's son, Luke Murray, has been an assistant coach under head coach Dan Hurley since 2021, helping the Huskies win consecutive national championships in 2023 and 2024. The 75-year-old Murray has regularly attended games during that time and even celebrated on the court with the team after their title wins. Why it matters Bill Murray's fandom and involvement with the UConn basketball program has added an extra layer of celebrity and excitement around the Huskies' recent success. As one of the most recognizable actors in the world, Murray's presence at games has helped raise the profile of the program and the sport of college basketball. The details Luke Murray, Bill Murray's son, joined the UConn coaching staff in 2021 after previously working as an assistant at Xavier University. Under head coach Dan Hurley, the Huskies have won back-to-back national championships in 2023 and 2024, with Luke Murray playing a key role in the team's success. Bill Murray has been a regular fixture at UConn home games during this run, often seen celebrating with the team after big wins. Luke Murray joined the UConn coaching staff in 2021.UConn won the national championship in 2023 and 2024. The players Bill MurrayA legendary American actor known for films like Ghostbusters, Groundhog Day, and Lost in Translation.Luke MurrayBill Murray's son, who has been an assistant coach for the UConn Huskies men's basketball team since 2021.Dan HurleyThe head coach of the UConn Huskies men's basketball team, who has led the team to consecutive national championships in 2023 and 2024. Got photos? Submit your photos here. › What they’re saying “Bill Murray is an absolute legend of an actor and many other things, but if you're watching the UConn Huskies play in the 2026 men's NCAA tournament, you may be wondering: Why is he rooting for UConn?”— Charles Curtis, Writer What’s next The UConn Huskies will look to continue their recent success and make another deep run in the 2026 NCAA tournament, with Bill Murray cheering them on from the stands. The takeaway Bill Murray's personal connection to the UConn basketball program through his son Luke has made him a beloved figure among Huskies fans. His enthusiastic support and celebration of the team's championships has added an extra layer of excitement and star power to the program's recent dominance.",
